cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in academic work, please cite both this
  repository and the underlying algorithmic spec (DFGHILM 2011 and
  Gaborit 1996). The first reproducible-from-source enumerations of
  doubly even binary linear codes at lengths beyond every published
  table were computed with this software: [29, k] (239,465,540
  classes) on 2026-05-23 and [30, k] (3,786,528,214 classes) on
  2026-06-15, each mass-formula certified at every rank — see
  docs/results/n30.json and docs/results/n29.json.
title: "doubly-even — enumerator of doubly even binary linear codes [N, k]"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Robert
    family-names: Eager
repository-code: "https://github.com/rdeager/doubly-even"
url: "https://github.com/rdeager/doubly-even"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0+n30"
commit: d074d01c6696e89281840dc5a25628e81a7453de
date-released: 2026-06-15
keywords:
  - doubly-even codes
  - binary linear codes
  - canonical augmentation
  - graph isomorphism
  - nauty
  - sparsenauty
  - DFGHILM
  - Adinkra
  - chromotopology
  - supersymmetry
